                        <div class="zwc-accordion_head">
                          <h4>What is an energy management system?</h4>
                          <span class="zwc-ent">&nbsp;</span>
                        </div>
                        <div class="zwc-accordion-content">
                          An energy management system (EMS) is end-to-end
                          software that can control, manage, and monitor the
                          energy consumption of your portfolios around the
                          globe. Intuitive visualization of your energy data at
                          a fundamental and granular level empowers you to track
                          every watt and leak.
                        </div>
                      </div>
                      <div class="zwc-accordion">
                        <div class="zwc-accordion_head">
                          <h4>Why should businesses choose an EMS?</h4>
                          <span class="zwc-ent">&nbsp;</span>
                        </div>
                        <div class="zwc-accordion-content">
                          Some of the reasons why companies, irrespective of
                          industry and size, are opting for an EMS is to enhance
                          sustainability, reduce operational costs, ensure
                          regulatory compliance, and improve environmental
                          impact while boosting their reputation and efficiency.
                        </div>
                      </div>
                      <div class="zwc-accordion">
                        <div class="zwc-accordion_head">
                          <h4>Who should use an EMS?</h4>
                          <span class="zwc-ent">&nbsp;</span>
                        </div>
                        <div class="zwc-accordion-content">
                          Any organization, regardless of size or industry, can
                          benefit from implementing an EMS to manage its
                          environmental responsibilities effectively.
                        </div>
                      </div>
                      <div class="zwc-accordion">
                        <div class="zwc-accordion_head">
                          <h4>What are the benefits of implementing an EMS?</h4>
                          <span class="zwc-ent">&nbsp;</span>
                        </div>
                        <div class="zwc-accordion-content">
                          Some of the benefits include reducing energy
                          consumption and wastage, compliance with environmental
                          laws, cost savings, improved resource efficiency, and
                          a stronger corporate image.
                        </div>
                      </div>
                      <div class="zwc-accordion">
                        <div class="zwc-accordion_head">
                          <h4>
                            How does an EMS help with regulatory compliance?
                          </h4>
                          <span class="zwc-ent">&nbsp;</span>
                        </div>
                        <div class="zwc-accordion-content">
                          An EMS ensures businesses meet environmental
                          regulations by monitoring, managing, and documenting
                          compliance, reducing the risk of penalties.
                        </div>
